<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hrvoje's Missal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1404</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Missal of Hrvoje</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hrvoje's Missal is a Croatian liturgical book written in the Glagolitic script around 1403–1404 in Split for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hrvoje-vukcic-hrvatinic">Hrvoje Vukčić Hrvatinić</a>, Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and Duke of Split. Copied by the scribe Butko, it is richly illuminated with miniatures in a mixed Gothic and Byzantine style. It is one of the finest Croatian medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> and is kept in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/topkapi-palace">Topkapı Palace</a> library in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hrvojes-missal.jpg" alt="Hrvoje's Missal" width="320" height="653" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Glagolitic scribe Butko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hrvoje%27s_missal_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
